  "problem": "Consider a $7\\times 9$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=3,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T}))=$",
  "worked_solution": "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14093810/assets/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=7,$ $n=9,$ and $n-r=3.$ \n\nSubstituting $n=9$ into $n-r=3,$ we can find the rank of $A:$\n\n$$\n(9)-r=3\\,\u27f9\\,r=6\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T})) & =r=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
